# "Counter target spell": with Bot1's Duress and, above it, Haywire Mite's activated ability (exiling Bot2's Mox Jet) on the stack, Bot2's Miscalculation cannot target the ability (refusal) but can target Duress
# (the positive control), which Bot1 then pays {2} for... it cannot, so Duress is countered while the ability still resolves.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Haywire Mite
Mox Emerald
Duress
Forest
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Miscalculation
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Haywire Mite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Duress.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Haywire Mite.Activate(Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet)
! Bot2.Hand.Miscalculation.Cast(Stack.Haywire Mite)
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Miscalculation.Cast(Duress)
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Duress; Haywire Mite
Exile = Mox Jet
Bot2.Graveyard = Miscalculation
